{"diagnosis":"The previous patch referenced a non-existent field `processList` on the SystemInfo.getProcessInfo return value. Per verified local primary source D:/projects/npm-cache/_npx/cbf1b8a072280925/node_modules/playwright-core/types/protocol.d.ts lines 18565-18570, `getProcessInfoReturnValue = { processInfo: ProcessInfo[] }` — the field is `processInfo`, an array. The previous patch also detached only after filtering, had no array/type check on the response, no PID sanity check, and misclassified schema/PID failures as generic 'BLOCKED'.","old":"const info = await cdp.send('SystemInfo.getProcessInfo');
    const browserProcs = info.processList.filter(p => p.type === 'browser');
    if (browserProcs.length !== 1) throw { classify: 'BLOCKED', msg: 'browser pid ambiguous' };
    const browserPid = browserProcs[0].id;
    await cdp.detach();","new":"const resp = await cdp.send('SystemInfo.getProcessInfo');
    await cdp.detach();
    if (!Array.isArray(resp.processInfo)) throw { classify: 'BLOCKED_DRIVER', msg: 'getProcessInfo: processInfo is not an array', rawResp: resp };
    const browserProcs = resp.processInfo.filter(p => p.type === 'browser');
    if (browserProcs.length !== 1) throw { classify: 'BLOCKED_DRIVER', msg: 'browser pid ambiguous', rawResp: resp };
    const browserPid = browserProcs[0].id;
    if (!Number.isSafeInteger(browserPid) || browserPid <= 0) throw { classify: 'BLOCKED_DRIVER', msg: 'browser pid is not a positive safe integer', rawResp: resp };","reason":"Corrected field name to `processInfo` per the verified protocol.d.ts definition. `cdp.detach()` now runs immediately after send so the CDP session is not held during validation; the already-received `resp` object remains readable after detach. The raw response is preserved verbatim on every failure path (`rawResp: resp`) and no failure is swallowed — all schema/PID violations throw with classification 'BLOCKED_DRIVER'. Validation enforces: processInfo is an array, exactly one browser-type entry, and a positive safe integer PID.","classification":"BLOCKED_DRIVER","cleanupReplacement":"t.close = async () => {
  writeResults();
  await ctx.close();
  const remaining = ctx.pages();
  if (remaining.length !== 0) {
    throw new Error(`task context close incomplete: ${remaining.length} page(s) remain after ctx.close()`);
  }
  return { ownedContextCloseCompleted: true, pagesRemaining: 0 };
};"}
